Epilogue 1
I hear the shield make a terrifying cracking sound.
(t): This could get pretty dangerous!
I grit my teeth while holding onto the shield with all my strength, but the force that is thrown against me only seems to get larger.
(t): This is bad! I have to make sure Scarlet is safe first.
I yell at the top of my lungs.
Me: Get out of here, quick!
Amon whirls around.
It looks like he just remembered that his objective is back there.
Scarlet puts up a fight but the guys manage to drag her away.
Amon is about to go after them, but I grab him by his shirt.
Me: Oh no, you won't!
Then one final hit from the spirit smashes the shield into a million pieces and I feel a weird sensation in my body.
At first it's scorching hot but then it only leaves a cold chill behind.
My vision fades away.
Me: Scar… let…
(SCARLET POV, NEW SCENE, NO SCARLET SPRITE, ME = SCARLET)
I'm dragged out of the basement by Seth and Ray.
Me: Let me go! I can't just leave {playerName} there! What if something happens?
Lu closes the door behind him.
Lu: We don't have the power to go against that.
(t): I don't care right now. If anything happens to {playerName} I could never forgive myself. The fight against the Interdimensional Spirits is enough trouble already, but because of me, Amon is here as well.
I am about to tell them off, but before I can say anything we hear a loud bang from the basement.
Me: What… was that?
Silence.
Ray: Boss, I have a bad feelin'!
Seth tries to usher me further towards the exit but then the basement door opens with a creak.
We look back.
Me: {playerName}?
(t): It's {playerName} right? I'm glad they're alive.
I can't even begin to describe the relief that washes over me.
But in the next moment it all comes crashing down.
Amon appears in the door frame.
He's holding his silver sword, which has already injured Seth and the others in the brawl before {playerName} arrived here.
Seth: Boss, we have to hurry. Or else we won't make it out alive.
Me: No! Where's {playerName}?
Ray: Seth! Lu! Get the boss outta here. Leave the scumbag to me.
Me: Wait! what about {playerName}???
Amon starts laughing maniacally.
Amon: This is why it's worth making a deal with the devil. I get to travel back and forth in time, and the devil even kills people for me!
(t): He's speaking as if {playerName} is dead. That can't be.
Lu: Boss, please! Let's go!
Me: Shut up! It can't be! You wouldn't be able to defeat someone like {playerName}!
Amon lunges forward with incredible speed and pierces through Ray's stomach with the sword.
Lu: Ray!
(t): What was that? I've never seen him move like this before.
I see pain and sadness contorting Seth's face.
Seth: Boss.
Amon: You're right, my dear Scarlet. I wouldn't have been able to defeat that weird friend of yours. But that devil did. And I might have borrowed some of its power.
(t): No, it seems like it turned him mad.
There is not an ounce of sanity left in Amon's eyes.
I feel my knees weaken.
The reality starts to sink in.
(t): {playerName} is dead? and Ray as well.
I feel a vast emptiness in my chest, like a part of it has been ripped out.
I see Lu quietly shedding tears an then step between me and Amon.
Amon sees this as a sign to attack and makes another swift movement.
A second later I see Lu's head rolling on the floor.
(t): This must be a night mare. It can't be real.
Seth: Boss! Boss!
Why does he sound so muffled?
He tries to pull me further away, but I can't move a muscle.
Then Amon lunges forward again and finally kills Seth, who has thrown his body in front of me, trying to shield me from the blade.
I sink to the ground.
(t): Why?
I want to cry. But no tears are coming out.
I want to scream. But not a sound leaves my mouth.
Amon: I don't even need your stupid marriage anymore. Thanks to you, I managed to come to the future. I'm going to have plenty of fun here even without you.
He looks down at me.
Amon: Though, it would be nice to keep you as a memento. You know? For old time's sake.
He grins at me and I feel like throwing up.
But yet again, nothing comes out.
Amon picks me up and takes my limp body back into the basement and into a confinement room.
ILLUSTRATION
Amon: This will be our new life from now on.
He takes my hand and whispers in my ear.
Amon: Until death do us part.
THE END
